# Secrets. Locally: copy to .dev.vars. On Cloudflare: `npx wrangler secret put NAME` for each one you use.
# Never commit real values.

# GitHub App (recommended, read-only): its ID and the whole private key (.pem).
GITHUB_APP_ID=
GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Or instead of an App: a fine-grained personal access token, read-only.
GITHUB_TOKEN=
# The webhook's secret (the App's, or the organisation webhook's). Several, comma-separated, while rotating.
GITHUB_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
# With AUTH=github: the OAuth app (the GitHub App's own client ID and secret work) and a 32+ character random secret.
GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GITHUB_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
SESSION_SECRET=

# Qubi, the reviewer (optional; README, docs/setup.md step 6). Your own model key, and a second GitHub App that may
# comment and open pull requests (Contents and Pull requests, read and write). Nothing runs until it is switched on.
QUBI_API_KEY=
QUBI_GITHUB_APP_ID=
QUBI_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
# Or instead of Qubi's App: a fine-grained token with the same permissions.
QUBI_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# Who may change Qubi's settings and start paid runs: GitHub logins or emails, comma-separated.
QUBI_ADMINS=
